    "result_text": "The build is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the welcome notification on successful owner create.\n\n**New function class** \u2014 `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/NotifyOwnerWelcome.java`: emits via the `NOTIFY` logger a line carrying the owner id and `memberId`, mirroring the existing `AuditOwnerCreated` pattern.\n\n```java\nprivate static final Logger NOTIFY = LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"NOTIFY\");\n\npublic void service(@Val Owner owner) {\n    NOTIFY.info(\"Welcome owner id={} memberId={}\", owner.getId(), owner.getMemberId());\n}\n```\n\n**Pipeline wiring** \u2014 `src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`: inserted a `notifyWelcome` step after `audit` and before `respond`, so it runs only after the owner is persisted (id assigned) and the create succeeds:\n\n```yaml\naudit:\n  class: ...AuditOwnerCreated\n  next: notifyWelcome\nnotifyWelcome:\n  class: ...NotifyOwnerWelcome\n  next: respond\n```\n\nThe step takes the pipeline-threaded `@Val Owner`, so both the id and the already-assigned `memberId` are available. The target test `AcceptanceTest.coreEnqueuesWelcome` passes and the full suite is **BUILD SUCCESS** (observed log line: `INFO NOTIFY - Welcome owner id=11 memberId=NSW2716E6609E1`).",
